o","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":345,"closed_issues":2336,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-04-13T15:59:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T08:21:32Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-09-10T23:13:00Z","updated_at":"2026-10-05T15:59:34Z","closed_at":"2026-10-05T15:59:34Z","assignee":{"login":"QbieShay","id":7917475,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MTc0NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7917475?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay","html_url":"https://github.com/QbieShay","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.8.dev cb41ea115\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.8.dev (cb41ea115) - Fedora Linux 44 (KDE Plasma Desktop Edition) on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor (3840x2160 @ 240.02 Hz) - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5090 (nvidia; 610.57.04) - AMD Ryzen 9 9950X3D 16-Core Processor (32 threads) - 62.33 GiB memory - PulseAudio (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nA static Trail3D does not update when width or color is changed if Limit Mode was changed from Time to Length. By \"static\", I mean a Trail3D that isn't being actively moved somehow.\n\nIt updates when you change the width curve or color curve (but not when you initially add a new Curve or Gradient resource, or replace it with another one).\n\nThese properties are affected:\n\n- Width\n- Width Curve\n- Color\n- Color Gradient\n- Tiling Mode\n- Tiling Multiplier\n- Pin UV\n\n(**Min Section Length** intentionally doesn't affect existing parts of the trail, so it's working as intended.)\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9a01e696-f9c6-449f-8378-a236e8f80b28\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Add a Trail3D node.\n- Change its **Limit Mode** from Time to Length. *This is important as the bug doesn't reproduce if you load a saved scene where the limit mode is already Length.*\n- Move the Trail3D node around to make the trail visible.\n- Change one of the properties listed above. Notice how there are no visible changes in the 3D viewport.\n- Move the Trail3D node around, and notice the trail updating.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[test_trail_3d_update.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/32079889/test_trail_3d_update.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ